Package: conch
Version: @VERSION@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Tom Laird-McConnell <thermous@iciclecreek.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, zlib1g,
 libssl3t64 | libssl3 | libssl1.1,
 libicu76 | libicu74 | libicu72 | libicu71 | libicu70 | libicu67
Recommends: kmscon
Homepage: https://github.com/tomlm/Conch
Description: TUI application shell for terminal applications
 Conch is a windowing environment for terminal applications. It hosts
 multiple XTerm terminal windows inside a single console session, so a
 machine with no graphical stack still gets overlapping, movable,
 resizable windows.
 .
 Applications are described by YAML registration files declaring how to
 install, detect and launch them. A seed catalog ships with the package
 and is refreshed from an upstream feed.
 .
 This package ships conch@.service, a getty-style template unit that runs
 Conch on a tty. It is not enabled by default; enable conch@tty1.service
 to take over the first console.
